(286253, 19091, 6150, '<td valign="top">Great shot.  I can''t find one thing wrong with it.  You deserve a good score with this one.  Good luck!!!</td>', 'Great shot.  I can''t find one thing wrong with it.  You deserve a good score with this one.  Good luck!!!', '2003-05-02 18:40:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(286256, 19232, 8320, '<td valign="top">Brilliant</td>', 'Brilliant', '2003-05-02 18:42:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(286260, 19480, 1005, '<td valign="top">All well taken images.  The center one is a bit hard to tell what it is, but the others seem pretty recognizable.  Seems more like that latter half "Life of Steel", how about Rust Starts Here?  It''s a nice collection of shots, but I''m having a hard time getting into it.   7 Rob the Swash</td>', 'All well taken images.  The center one is a bit hard to tell what it is, but the others seem pretty recognizable.  Seems more like that latter half "Life of Steel", how about Rust Starts Here?  It''s a nice collection of shots, but I''m having a hard time getting into it.   7 Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:00:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(286262, 19250, 1280, '<td valign="top">Very nice work!</td>', 'Very nice work!', '2003-05-02 19:03:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(286265, 19406, 1005, '<td valign="top">Good collection of train parts.  I like the top frame best.  The middle frame seems a tad over exposed, the red seems so bright as to be unnatural (but I''m going to assume the painter found a VERY bright paint).  Lower frame has some parts that seem over exposed, too (same silver colored parts).  This is a difficult challenge due to the small frames needed.  You got close enough for nice details, maybe too close to get a feel for the machinery.  Very hard to call (too close vs not enough detail), I honestly think you did pretty well.  7 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Good collection of train parts.  I like the top frame best.  The middle frame seems a tad over exposed, the red seems so bright as to be unnatural (but I''m going to assume the painter found a VERY bright paint).  Lower frame has some parts that seem over exposed, too (same silver colored parts).  This is a difficult challenge due to the small frames needed.  You got close enough for nice details, maybe too close to get a feel for the machinery.  Very hard to call (too close vs not enough detail), I honestly think you did pretty well.  7 Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:05:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(286267, 19643, 1005, '<td valign="top">Nice series!  I really like the two cells on the left, good feeling for trains coming and going.  The upper right frame is very good with extremely difficult lighting, but it doesn''t show me what they are doing (keeping the audience guessing might be a good thing, but I doubt it).  The lower right frame is well focused, but the overcast takes away quite a bit of the spendor (maybe shotting this more level would have looked better).  7 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Nice series!  I really like the two cells on the left, good feeling for trains coming and going.  The upper right frame is very good with extremely difficult lighting, but it doesn''t show me what they are doing (keeping the audience guessing might be a good thing, but I doubt it).  The lower right frame is well focused, but the overcast takes away quite a bit of the spendor (maybe shotting this more level would have looked better).  7 Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:09:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(286269, 19278, 1005, '<td valign="top">Neat idea!  Very clear shots.  Lighting is harsh and glaring.  The angled views of the cars is very nice.  This is a bit of a nit (and probably asking for too much), but two Porsches and a Toyota?  I would suggest more variety or less (no points involved at all).  7 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Neat idea!  Very clear shots.  Lighting is harsh and glaring.  The angled views of the cars is very nice.  This is a bit of a nit (and probably asking for too much), but two Porsches and a Toyota?  I would suggest more variety or less (no points involved at all).  7 Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:12:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(286270, 19636, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice shots, great amounts of detail.  (The flowers look almost too wet.)  I really like the lighting on the 2nd and 3rd cells, the first is pretty good, but a tad glaring at the top.  Focus seems pretty sharp, too bad the narsissus'' outer petals reach out of focus, but camera reality (I hope the viewers don''t fixate on that too much).  Without the glare spot, this is a 10.  High 9 - Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very nice shots, great amounts of detail.  (The flowers look almost too wet.)  I really like the lighting on the 2nd and 3rd cells, the first is pretty good, but a tad glaring at the top.  Focus seems pretty sharp, too bad the narsissus'' outer petals reach out of focus, but camera reality (I hope the viewers don''t fixate on that too much).  Without the glare spot, this is a 10.  High 9 - Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:15:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(286271, 19221, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice series!  Good detail and nice imagination to come up with this!  The lower cell is just fine, emulates flight well.  It would have been truly impossible to catch them in real flight, but I would have liked it a touch better (how many years to do this???).  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very nice series!  Good detail and nice imagination to come up with this!  The lower cell is just fine, emulates flight well.  It would have been truly impossible to catch them in real flight, but I would have liked it a touch better (how many years to do this???).  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:18:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(286274, 19750, 1005, '<td valign="top">It''s a beautiful place!  I would have reversed the two left shots, but this is a clockwise display (so your choice is probably better!).  Upper left cell has an unnatural series of archs in the water color (probably from the sun), not a good thing.  The willow trees and their reflections are very nice.  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'It''s a beautiful place!  I would have reversed the two left shots, but this is a clockwise display (so your choice is probably better!).  Upper left cell has an unnatural series of archs in the water color (probably from the sun), not a good thing.  The willow trees and their reflections are very nice.  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:22:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(286275, 19358, 1280, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done.  Very emotive.  I love it!</td>', 'Beautifully done.  Very emotive.  I love it!', '2003-05-02 19:22:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(286276, 19106, 1280, '<td valign="top">Two of the images are very nice.  The middle one is too dark, and doesn''t fit really.</td>', 'Two of the images are very nice.  The middle one is too dark, and doesn''t fit really.', '2003-05-02 19:24:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(286277, 19652, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice!  Great contrast, your lighting is nearly above reproach!  (a slight bright spot on the left boy''s left forehead)  A true (non-score affecting) NIT - the left boy''s lips are downturned....(I told you it was a NIT).  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very nice!  Great contrast, your lighting is nearly above reproach!  (a slight bright spot on the left boy''s left forehead)  A true (non-score affecting) NIT - the left boy''s lips are downturned....(I told you it was a NIT).  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:26:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(286278, 19685, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very, very cool idea!!  The execution is nearly perfect, too.  Was this one image divided or three separate shots?  (I think it''s three, but it''s hard to say for certain)  The strings of the "still" balls seem to have a bit of motion.  Here''s a complete nit for you...the shadows of the outside still balls aren''t quite parallel with the other four (really, no score impact, just pointing out a tiny, insignificant flaw)  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very, very cool idea!!  The execution is nearly perfect, too.  Was this one image divided or three separate shots?  (I think it''s three, but it''s hard to say for certain)  The strings of the "still" balls seem to have a bit of motion.  Here''s a complete nit for you...the shadows of the outside still balls aren''t quite parallel with the other four (really, no score impact, just pointing out a tiny, insignificant flaw)  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:30:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(286279, 19662, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice scene!  Was this three shots or one separated?  (It does NOT matter, just curious, I think it''s one shot)  Nice dramatic cloudy sky (is this somewhere on the Puget Sound? or otherwise near me?)  The one crashing wave is nice, but the rest of the water seems a bit too calm (now, isn''t that asking for the sun, moon and the stars....no score impact).  The rocks on the lower left seem a bit dark (duh, it''s a cloudy day....).  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very nice scene!  Was this three shots or one separated?  (It does NOT matter, just curious, I think it''s one shot)  Nice dramatic cloudy sky (is this somewhere on the Puget Sound? or otherwise near me?)  The one crashing wave is nice, but the rest of the water seems a bit too calm (now, isn''t that asking for the sun, moon and the stars....no score impact).  The rocks on the lower left seem a bit dark (duh, it''s a cloudy day....).  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:34:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(286280, 19613, 1005, '<td valign="top">Really neat series!  It matched up pretty well with the outer panels at an angle, but not with the building (I think these angled cells add more interest, even if they don''t match up exactly, but a perfect shot would have matched it all using a tripod with a flex head. 9 Rob the Swash (and anthropologist!)</td>', 'Really neat series!  It matched up pretty well with the outer panels at an angle, but not with the building (I think these angled cells add more interest, even if they don''t match up exactly, but a perfect shot would have matched it all using a tripod with a flex head. 9 Rob the Swash (and anthropologist!)', '2003-05-02 19:37:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(286281, 19550, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very cool shot!  I really like the fog hanging on the lake!  The silhouetted trees are very nice.  I''m liking this better and better....score upgrade from 9 to 10!  Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very cool shot!  I really like the fog hanging on the lake!  The silhouetted trees are very nice.  I''m liking this better and better....score upgrade from 9 to 10!  Rob the Swash', '2003-05-02 19:39:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(286297, 19759, 3579, '<td valign="top">Interesting eye study. The lighting and exposure is really well done. One thing that I think is necessary in this kind of composition is to accurately align the frames. The two on the left are marginally higher than they should be, and the one in the bottom left corner is a little smaller than its counterpart.</td>', 'Interesting eye study. The lighting and exposure is really well done. One thing that I think is necessary in this kind of composition is to accurately align the frames. The two on the left are marginally higher than they should be, and the one in the bottom left corner is a little smaller than its counterpart.', '2003-05-02 20:57:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(286328, 19406, 3607, '<td valign="top">fun photo(s).  i think if you had not cropped in so closely on the bottom one that one would have come out a little stronger as the wheels seem almost too tight, but cool idea overall.</td>', 'fun photo(s).  i think if you had not cropped in so closely on the bottom one that one would have come out a little stronger as the wheels seem almost too tight, but cool idea overall.', '2003-05-02 23:01:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(286329, 19106, 3607, '<td valign="top">the cropping seems a little tight, esp. on the middle one, but the overall theme is great and the combination is well done.</td>', 'the cropping seems a little tight, esp. on the middle one, but the overall theme is great and the combination is well done.', '2003-05-02 23:02:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(286330, 19641, 3607, '<td valign="top">fantastic photos.  my only complaint is on the combination of the photos re: alignment/borders - i think the overall effect would have been more powerful if you had not cropped the side photos smaller than the middle one, and if you had used consistent borders around all of the shots.</td>', 'fantastic photos.  my only complaint is on the combination of the photos re: alignment/borders - i think the overall effect would have been more powerful if you had not cropped the side photos smaller than the middle one, and if you had used consistent borders around all of the shots.', '2003-05-02 23:03:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(286331, 19448, 3607, '<td valign="top">these are great!  nicely combined and the best use of text in a photo i''ve seen so far.  10</td>', 'these are great!  nicely combined and the best use of text in a photo i''ve seen so far.  10', '2003-05-02 23:04:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(286332, 19415, 3607, '<td valign="top">the photos are very nice.  the alignment is a bit off at the bottom of the middle photo, and for your choice of the third photo it might have been even more powerful if you had the lake w/no boat in it.</td>', 'the photos are very nice.  the alignment is a bit off at the bottom of the middle photo, and for your choice of the third photo it might have been even more powerful if you had the lake w/no boat in it.', '2003-05-02 23:06:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(286334, 19177, 3607, '<td valign="top">very fun and each individual photo is very well shot.  this is also a very subtlely entered photo, with 1) mom and pop, 2) mom and pop DOING IT ON FILM!, 3) mom and pop w/kids.  i wonder if everyone caught this . . .</td>', 'very fun and each individual photo is very well shot.  this is also a very subtlely entered photo, with 1) mom and pop, 2) mom and pop DOING IT ON FILM!, 3) mom and pop w/kids.  i wonder if everyone caught this . . .', '2003-05-02 23:08:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(286336, 19751, 3607, '<td valign="top">i think the photos are fine and combined well, but the story being told isn''t very clear.</td>', 'i think the photos are fine and combined well, but the story being told isn''t very clear.', '2003-05-02 23:09:53.000000', NULL, 1),
