(287494, 19587, 7901, '<td valign="top">With this I wanted to try and make a trail from shot to shot for the eye to follow. Not sure exactly how successful it was. But, starting at the left frame, the lower left side. Going up and around to the top left of the second frame. Going down along the line to the bottom of the third frame. Then up to the drain. For me it was all about a beginning and an end. This subject and location was used to catch some off-guard. As you don''t readily expect to see this in a bathroom.<br/> <br/>The blood was Hershey''s Chocolate Syrup. I never thought the smell of chocolate could become nauseating, but if there''s enough of it, I guess it could. The deal with the second frame was I thought I left enough for myself to work with on the crop. But when it came down to it, I fudged. The background on it, even blurred; to me seems too distracting. <br/> <br/>Thank you everyone who commented. Appreciate the time you took :)<br/> <br/>matt<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-05-10 01:26:19.</i></td>', 'With this I wanted to try and make a trail from shot to shot for the eye to follow. Not sure exactly how successful it was. But, starting at the left frame, the lower left side. Going up and around to the top left of the second frame. Going down along the line to the bottom of the third frame. Then up to the drain. For me it was all about a beginning and an end. This subject and location was used to catch some off-guard. As you don''t readily expect to see this in a bathroom. The blood was Hershey''s Chocolate Syrup. I never thought the smell of chocolate could become nauseating, but if there''s enough of it, I guess it could. The deal with the second frame was I thought I left enough for myself to work with on the crop. But when it came down to it, I fudged. The background on it, even blurred; to me seems too distracting.  Thank you everyone who commented. Appreciate the time you took :) matt', '2003-05-05 01:15:34.000000', '2003-05-10 02:26:19.000000', 0),
