(288036, 19264, 6451, '<td valign="top">good job. nice pic.</td>', 'good job. nice pic.', '2003-05-05 14:35:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(288143, 19726, 714, '<td valign="top">Ok you want my honest opinion.  I don''t like this because of the red/yellow tones.  The face on the upper right is way out of focus and to blurry.  I do like the text and the way you put the lined the pictures.  Maybe use more lighting and then make it black/white and then put some red/yellow tint to it.  It would make the picture more clear and give you the color you want.  Of course I haven''t tried it so I am not sure it would work.  <br/>I did something similar with my "despair" picture.</td>', 'Ok you want my honest opinion.  I don''t like this because of the red/yellow tones.  The face on the upper right is way out of focus and to blurry.  I do like the text and the way you put the lined the pictures.  Maybe use more lighting and then make it black/white and then put some red/yellow tint to it.  It would make the picture more clear and give you the color you want.  Of course I haven''t tried it so I am not sure it would work.  I did something similar with my "despair" picture.', '2003-05-05 15:22:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(288188, 19569, 472, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments.<br/> <br/>To Tony Ku: I just took a pic of the characters on the planter and used those as a design motif.  Which is no different from showing a picture of the planter itself.  If you have a problem with that you should take it up with the manufacturers of that planter.  Let me know when they respond to your letter and what the response is.  <br/> <br/>Re: "zen": sorry but zen has a lot of colloquial meanings that arent necessarily connected with a religious dogma, that include meditation, peace, inner calm, enlightenment, desirelessness, etc.  To me, this picture is evocative of those meanings.  I can''t imagine that such a usage would give offense, but if it did, my sincere apologies.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-05-05 16:43:43.</i></td>', 'Thanks for your comments. To Tony Ku: I just took a pic of the characters on the planter and used those as a design motif.  Which is no different from showing a picture of the planter itself.  If you have a problem with that you should take it up with the manufacturers of that planter.  Let me know when they respond to your letter and what the response is.   Re: "zen": sorry but zen has a lot of colloquial meanings that arent necessarily connected with a religious dogma, that include meditation, peace, inner calm, enlightenment, desirelessness, etc.  To me, this picture is evocative of those meanings.  I can''t imagine that such a usage would give offense, but if it did, my sincere apologies.', '2003-05-05 15:58:41.000000', '2003-05-05 17:43:43.000000', 0),
